Intact skin with a localized area of non-blanchable erythema, which may 
appear differently in darkly pigmented skin. Presence of blanchable 
erythema or changes in sensation, temperature, or firmness may precede 
visual changes. Color changes do not include purple or maroon 
discoloration; these may indicate deep tissue pressure injury.
