<FILEMAN_FILE>
<FILE_NAME>REMINDER DIALOG</FILE_NAME>
<FILE_NUMBER>801.41</FILE_NUMBER>
<POINT_01>VA-EL PRESSURE INJURY INFORMATION</POINT_01>
<INTERNAL_ENTRY_NUMBER>29475</INTERNAL_ENTRY_NUMBER>
<CHECKSUM>2093133981</CHECKSUM>
<SELECTED>NO</SELECTED>
<FILEMAN_FDA>
<![CDATA[
801.41;+29475,;.01~VA-EL PRESSURE INJURY INFORMATION
801.41;+29475,;4~dialog element
801.41;+29475,;23~YES
801.41;+29475,;25~WP-start~7
A pressure injury is localized damage to the skin and underlying soft 
tissue usually over a bony prominence or related to a medical or other 
device.  The injury can present as intact skin or an open ulcer and may 
be painful. The injury occurs as a result of intense and/or prolonged 
pressure or pressure in combination with shear. The tolerance of soft 
tissue for pressure and shear may also be affected by microclimate, 
nutrition, perfusion, co-morbidities and condition of the soft tissue.
801.41;+29475,;51~SUPPRESS
801.41;+29475,;100~NATIONAL
801.41;+29475,;101~Office of Nursing Service
801.44;+29476,+29475,;.01~04/30/2020@11:35:23
801.44;+29476,+29475,;2~WP-start~1
Exchange Stub
]]>
